/*
    For a set and an int, `A ^ n` denotes the set of n-tuples over `A`, which is `A` fused
    with itself n times.
    `string^3` is the set of three-tuples of strings, the same set as
    `string * string * string`.
    This is the same reading as the function case: `n` stands for the set of the first n
    index positions, and a tuple is a function from index to component.
*/

string^3
